$schema: https://usm.dev/schema/v1.json
$id: smith-gray/exec-wrapper
$type: feature
$version: 1
$last_updated: "2026-09-22"
summary: |
  `safekeys exec --token … -- <command>` runs a command with secrets injected into its environment
  and the ambient environment scrubbed. It is the framework-agnostic integration: any harness that
  can spawn a subprocess works immediately, and the caller receives only an exit code.
$system: smith-gray/system
$service: smith-gray/cli
status: built
intent: |
  The cleanest "the model never sees plaintext" path is the one where the secret never appears in
  any argument, output, or transcript the model can read. A wrapper that spawns the consumer as its
  own child, passes secrets through the child's environment, and returns only an exit code achieves
  that for every tool that already exists, with no SDK or framework integration required.
flows:
  - id: exec-with-token
    name: Execute a wrapped command
    description: The CLI resolves the token and runs the command with injected env.
    steps:
      - id: s1
        action: receive
        target: CLI receives a token and a command to run after a -- separator.
      - id: s2
        action: send
        target: CLI forwards the resolve request to the local sidecar over its socket.
      - id: s3
        action: setup
        target: >-
          Sidecar builds a minimal environment for the child, adds the injected value under its
          variable name, and spawns the command.
      - id: s4
        action: observe
        target: The command runs; its stdout and stderr are streamed to the caller.
      - id: s5
        action: receive
        target: The caller receives the command's exit code; the value is never printed by the wrapper.
contracts:
  - id: env-scrubbed
    description: The wrapped command must not inherit the full ambient environment.
    must_have:
      - The child gets a minimal, explicit environment
      - The child does not inherit the agent's or shell's full variable set
      - Only the requested secrets are added by name
  - id: exit-code-only
    description: The wrapper returns a status, never a value.
    must_have:
      - Success is communicated by exit code
      - The wrapper does not echo resolved values to stdout or stderr
      - Arguments to the wrapper never contain plaintext
  - id: token-not-plaintext-argv
    description: The command line carries a token, not a secret.
    must_have:
      - The token appears in argv, which is not sensitive
      - No plaintext ever appears in argv
      - Process listings reveal nothing sensitive
tests:
  - id: child-sees-injected-env
    flow: exec-with-token
    setup:
      command: sh -c 'test "$API_KEY" = "expected"'
    expect:
      - assertion: the command exits zero
      - assertion: the injected variable is present in the child environment
    contracts:
      - env-scrubbed
  - id: ambient-env-not-inherited
    flow: exec-with-token
    setup:
      ambient_var: SHOULD_NOT_APPEAR
    expect:
      - assertion: the child does not see ambient variables outside the explicit allowlist
    contracts:
      - env-scrubbed
  - id: no-plaintext-in-argv-or-output
    flow: exec-with-token
    setup:
      command: printenv API_KEY
    expect:
      - assertion: the wrapper's own output does not include the value
      - assertion: process arguments contain the token but not the value
    contracts:
      - exit-code-only
      - token-not-plaintext-argv
decisions:
  - id: exec-is-framework-agnostic
    decision: Ship the exec wrapper as a first-class MVP harness integration.
    rationale: >-
      The blueprint lists CLI/exec as one of three MVP integrations precisely because it is
      framework-agnostic — any harness that can spawn a subprocess works, including ones with no
      SDK. It is also the cleanest model-never-sees-plaintext path.
    status: accepted
  - id: minimal-env
    decision: >-
      Give the child a minimal, explicit environment rather than inheriting and augmenting the
      parent's.
    rationale: >-
      Inheritance is the classic leak vector — ambient credentials, tokens, and paths follow the
      process in silently. Allowlisting inverts the default to deny.
    status: accepted
implementation:
  primary: apps/cli/internal/commands/commands.go
  test_code: pkg/inject/inject_test.go
  test_code_status: manual
see_also:
  - smith-gray/secret-injection
  - smith-gray/python-sdk
  - smith-gray/mcp-server
